11:["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-introduction section-shell","id":"overview","aria-labelledby":"summary-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"paper-introduction-title","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"summary-title","children":"Multi-Agent Units of Responsibility for Authoring Long-Horizon Presentations"}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"paper-introduction-copy","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"paper-tldr","children":"Page ownership that carries through authoring, inspection, and revision. MURAL coordinates an HTML presentation through shared facts, design decisions, and persistent responsibility."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"paper-home-abstract","aria-labelledby":"abstract-title","children":[["$","h3",null,{"id":"abstract-title","children":"Abstract"}],[["$","p","Automated presentation generation requires accurate content, coherent narratives, and consistent visual semantics across slides. However, whole-deck authoring faces a growing context burden as execution histories accumulate, while independent per-slide authoring struggles to coordinate cross-slide dependencies. To address this, we introduce MuralPresenter, a multi-agent framework for long-horizon authoring of editable HTML presentations. The framework maintains a persistent shared deck state and adaptively assigns production responsibility to single-slide or slide-group agents based on joint authoring and revision needs. Each agent retains responsibility for generating, inspecting, and revising its assigned slides.",{"children":"Automated presentation generation requires accurate content, coherent narratives, and consistent visual semantics across slides. However, whole-deck authoring faces a growing context burden as execution histories accumulate, while independent per-slide authoring struggles to coordinate cross-slide dependencies. To address this, we introduce MuralPresenter, a multi-agent framework for long-horizon authoring of editable HTML presentations. The framework maintains a persistent shared deck state and adaptively assigns production responsibility to single-slide or slide-group agents based on joint authoring and revision needs. Each agent retains responsibility for generating, inspecting, and revising its assigned slides."}],["$","p","We adopt selective action supervision for model fine-tuning, retaining historical context while supervising only assistant messages newly generated within each execution segment. Our evaluation covers presentation generation, multi-turn editing, and requirement fulfillment across authoring stages.",{"children":"We adopt selective action supervision for model fine-tuning, retaining historical context while supervising only assistant messages newly generated within each execution segment. Our evaluation covers presentation generation, multi-turn editing, and requirement fulfillment across authoring stages."}],["$","p","With score-based output selection, MuralPresenter-27B obtains the highest PresentBench Overall score among the listed systems. The 9B model reaches 90.21% content accuracy on SlidesGen-Bench. On long decks, adaptive assignment improves mean final quality by 2.49 points over whole-deck production, with greater workload and a mean score comparable to per-slide assignment.",{"children":"With score-based output selection, MuralPresenter-27B obtains the highest PresentBench Overall score among the listed systems. The 9B model reaches 90.21% content accuracy on SlidesGen-Bench. On long decks, adaptive assignment improves mean final quality by 2.49 points over whole-deck production, with greater workload and a mean score comparable to per-slide assignment."}]]]}],"$L1c"]}]]}]
